---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <main>
    <section class="prd">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="section-tag">
          PRD
        </p>

        <h2>
          DineWise - AI Voice Concierge
        </h2>

        <p class="prd-intro">
          A completed product requirements document for a voice-first AI agent that turns
          natural-language dining preferences into personalized restaurant recommendations and
          real-time reservations through Swiggy Dineout MCP.
        </p>

        <div class="prd-meta">
          <span>Author: Gayatri Gupta</span>
          <span>Status: Completed</span>
          <span>Program: Swiggy Builders Club</span>
          <span>Target Release: NA</span>
        </div>

        <div class="prd-spec">
          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">01 · User Problem</span>
            <p>
              Restaurant booking apps are built around filters, but users think in experiences.
              They know the occasion, the atmosphere they want, their budget, and preferred
              timing - but not which restaurant best satisfies those constraints. The real
              friction isn't booking a table; it's confidently choosing one.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">02 · AI Value Proposition</span>
            <p>
              DineWise is a voice-first AI concierge built on Swiggy Dineout MCP. It transforms
              natural-language dining intent into personalized restaurant recommendations, checks
              live availability, and completes reservations through a single conversational
              experience.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">03 · Target User & Workflow</span>
            <p>
              The experience begins with a natural voice conversation, where the user simply
              describes the kind of dining experience they want. The AI extracts key preferences
              - including the occasion, ambience, budget, party size, and preferred timing -
              asks only one clarification when essential, searches Swiggy Dineout for matching
              restaurants and live availability, and recommends the best option. If the user
              changes a preference, the AI re-plans the recommendation while preserving the rest
              of the conversation before completing the reservation with confirmation.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">04 · Success Metric</span>
            <p>
              Reduce decision-making friction by replacing manual comparison across 20+
              restaurant listings with a single natural-language request that surfaces one
              confident, explainable restaurant recommendation.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">05 · Technical Architecture</span>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>AI Agent:</strong> Llama 3.2 (local via Ollama)</li>
              <li><strong>Commerce Layer:</strong> Swiggy Dineout MCP</li>
              <li><strong>Voice:</strong> Browser Speech-to-Text & Text-to-Speech</li>
              <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">06 · Voice-First Design Principle</span>
            <p>
              Voice experiences should reduce cognitive load, not read menus aloud. DineWise
              recommends at most three restaurants, speaks only the top match by default, and
              explains why it fits the user's intent instead of listing dozens of options.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">07 · Key Product Decisions</span>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Intent over filters:</strong> Maps implicit phrases like "somewhere we
                can actually talk" to ambience rather than keyword search.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Conversational re-planning:</strong> Updates only the modified preference
                (e.g. outdoor seating or budget) while preserving the rest of the conversation
                context.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Explainable AI:</strong> Every recommendation includes 2–3 factual
                reasons such as budget match, ambience, and live table availability.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="prd-spec-row">
            <span class="prd-spec-label">08 · Outcome</span>
            <p>
              DineWise demonstrates how AI agents can improve decision-making in commerce by
              turning restaurant discovery from a filter-based workflow into a natural
              conversation that understands intent, adapts to changing preferences, and completes
              reservations through Swiggy Dineout MCP.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>


<style>
.prd {
  padding: 120px 0 80px;
}

.prd-intro {
  color:var(--text-secondary);
  max-width:760px;
  font-size:1.05rem;
  margin-bottom:28px;
}

.prd-meta {
  display:flex;
  flex-wrap:wrap;
  gap:12px;
  margin-bottom:40px;
}

.prd-meta span {
  border:1px solid var(--border);
  color:var(--text-secondary);
  padding:8px 14px;
  border-radius:999px;
  font-size:0.9rem;
}

.prd-spec {
  border-top:1px solid var(--border);
}

.prd-spec-row {
  display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:280px 1fr;
  gap:40px;
  padding:26px 0;
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
}

.prd-spec-label {
  color:var(--accent);
  font-weight:700;
  font-size:0.95rem;
  letter-spacing:0.02em;
}

.prd-spec-row p {
  color:var(--text-secondary);
  max-width:640px;
}

.prd-spec-row p + p {
  margin-top:12px;
}

.prd-spec-row ul {
  color:var(--text-secondary);
  max-width:640px;
  padding-left:18px;
}

.prd-spec-row li {
  margin-bottom:10px;
}

.prd-spec-row li:last-child {
  margin-bottom:0;
}

.prd-spec-row li strong {
  color:var(--text-primary);
}

@media(max-width:800px){

  .prd {
    padding:100px 0 60px;
  }

  .prd-spec-row{
    grid-template-columns:1fr;
    gap:10px;
  }

}

@media(max-width:480px){

  .prd {
    padding:90px 0 60px;
  }

}
</style>
